.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-rollback 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-rollback \- List or restore a configuration backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut rollback\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISTAMP\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List or restore a configuration backup
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Color when writing to a terminal (default)
.IP \(bu 2
always: Color even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never color
.RE
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
List available backups
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the restore plan without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Restore without an interactive prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fISTAMP\fR]
Backup stamp to restore (defaults to the newest complete backup)
